# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Johnathan D. Georgaras et al. (2026). Accurate, transferable, and verifiable machine-learned interatomic potentials for layered materials.
#   Nature Communications. doi:10.1038/s41467-026-74482-2  arXiv:2503.15432v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2503.15432v1 (sha256 32d07d15846e7bf7...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 413 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/georgaras2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the split MLIP approach for MoS2/WSe2 bilayers: Allegro
# intralayer models for MoS2 and WSe2 (cutoff 6 A) trained on randomly
# perturbed 3x3 monolayer supercells and an Allegro interlayer model
# (cutoff 10 A) trained on stacking/separation scans, plus unified Allegro
# models UM1 (6 A) and UM2 (10 A) trained on the union, with the RMSEs
# stated in the text; Quantum ESPRESSO vdW-DF-C09 references. Test-set
# comparisons with classical SW and KC potentials (Fig. 2), the MDE
# metric, corruption analyses and HfS2/GaS relaxations are figure-only
# or properties.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
